# The Grey Mare (side quest, docs/story/side_quests.md): the black carriage that drives itself stopped by Radu's pen
# and left a purse. Radu sold it his grey mare, Steaua, because the voice in the carriage promised Nicu would ride
# home. She is tied at the Ivlis crossroads milestone, being finished into one of the castle's black horses, and the
# carriage fetches her at midnight. Reached from Zora's rumour (tser_camp:zora_road) and Radu (tser_camp:radu).
# Every line here is unvoiced for now.

~ asks
quest the_grey_mare asked
Narrator: Radu's smile arrives a moment late, like a man coming back from somewhere else.
Radu: Zora counts too much. Yes, I walked her down. Sold. A buyer came by, a buyer paid, and the horse goes to the buyer. That's horse-trading.
Radu: The buyer has a carriage and no driver, and you would like to know why I said yes. Everyone says yes to that carriage, friend. One day you'll say yes to it too.
* [Insight DC 14] It isn't the money, is it? -> why_read | why_unread
* [Persuasion DC 13] Why did you really sell her, Radu? -> why_read | why_unread
* Where is she now? -> where

~ why_unread
Narrator: He laughs and slaps the rail of the pen, and the laugh is good enough to fool a stranger, which is what you are.
-> where

~ why_read
set radu_bargain_known
quest the_grey_mare bargain
Radu [sad]: No. It isn't the money.
Radu: There was a voice in the carriage. Very kind. It said: give us the grey, and Nicu rides home tomorrow. Four days gone, my friend's boy, and the castle says he rides home if the grey goes to the crossroads tonight.
Radu: The castle doesn't lie about small things. That's how it gets you to believe it about the big ones.
* [if flag.crossroads_gallows_seen or flag.nicu_kin_told] (Tell him what hangs at the crossroads.) -> nicu_truth
* Where is she now? -> where

~ nicu_truth
set radu_knows_nicu
Narrator: You tell him about the gallows at the crossroads, and the board, and the two words on it. He listens with his hands flat on the rail.
Radu [angry]: Then I sold her for a rope. For a rope he was already wearing.
Radu: Bring her back. Bring her back and let the castle come and ask me why.
-> where

~ where
Radu: She's tied at the old milestone on the east side of the crossroads, where the roads meet. They fetch her at midnight. That's the bargain.
Radu: She won't stay grey, you understand. The carriage horses are black all through. They take a horse and they... finish it.
Radu: Her name's Steaua. She likes her ears scratched and she hates priests. If you're going, go.
-> END

# --- Radu at the camp, once the quest is under way (tser_camp:radu jumps here) ---

~ radu
if flag.mare_resolved
-> radu_after
endif
if flag.carriage_beaten and flag.mare_saved
-> return_saved
endif
if flag.carriage_beaten
-> return_lost
endif
if flag.mare_saved
Radu: She came down the road at a gallop an hour ago and went straight into the pen like she'd never left. Grey. All grey. What did you do? No, don't tell me. The carriage will be wanting a word with somebody.
-> END
endif
Radu: Midnight, friend. The old milestone, east side. Go, if you're going.
-> END

~ horses_without
Radu: Look at them. Plaited, brushed, fed better than the burgomaster of Vallaki.
Narrator: His eyes go to the empty place at the end of the pen and come back quickly.
Radu: Not for sale. None of them. Not today, not tomorrow.
-> END

~ return_saved
Narrator: Steaua is in the pen when you come back, grey as river stone, with Luminita's face pressed into her neck.
Radu: You broke the castle's bargain. Everyone in this camp is pretending they don't know who did it. That's the nicest thing Vistani can do for you.
if flag.radu_knows_nicu
Radu: And you told me the truth about Nicu, when the castle wouldn't. I owe you for that more than for the horse.
elif flag.radu_bargain_known
Radu: And still no Nicu on the road. The castle's promises keep about as well as its horses.
endif
Radu: Now. She was sold, so she isn't mine. And she was bought, so she isn't the castle's. Whose is she?
* She's yours, Radu. Never sell her again. -> to_radu
* Luminita's. She loves her best. -> to_luminita

~ to_radu
set mare_owner = "radu"
Radu: Mine. Then nobody gets her, ever, for any price. Not even for a good one.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +1 thistle +2: You brought Steaua home to Radu
-> reward

~ to_luminita
set mare_owner = "luminita"
attitude luminita friendly
Luminita: She was Nicu's favourite. He used to ride her bareback in the river and pretend he couldn't hear Radu shouting.
Luminita: Thank you. I'll keep her far away from the road.
Radu: That's fair. That's more than fair. That's the first fair thing to happen in this camp all week.
approve thistle +2 liriel_dawnsong +1 wren_featherfoot +1: You gave Steaua to Luminita, who loved her best
-> reward

~ return_lost
Narrator: Radu is standing at the empty end of the pen when you come back. He knows from your faces.
Radu: She's black now. Isn't she. And you had to put her down.
if flag.radu_knows_nicu
Radu: The castle took my friend's boy and my mare in one week, and it paid me in old gold for the mare. Not for the boy. It doesn't pay for those.
endif
Narrator: He ties a black ribbon to the gate, and doesn't say anything for a long time.
-> reward

~ reward
set mare_resolved
if flag.mare_saved
quest the_grey_mare home
else
quest the_grey_mare mourned
endif
Radu: Take the castle's gold. All of it. I don't want it in the camp.
gold +120
Radu: And this. A trader from over the mountains paid it for her, years ago, before I knew I'd never sell her. A bride price, he called it. It turns curses back, or so he swore. Better it goes with you.
give rod_of_the_pact_keeper_plus_1
-> END

~ radu_after
if flag.mare_owner == "radu"
Radu: She bit me this morning. First time ever. I deserved it.
elif flag.mare_owner == "luminita"
Radu: Luminita won't let me near her. Quite right.
else
Radu: Still no grey in the pen. I keep looking at the end where she stood.
endif
-> END

# --- Steaua at the crossroads milestone (prop grey_mare_milestone) ---

~ mare
if flag.mare_lost
Narrator: She is black from muzzle to tail now, and her eyes are coals in a banked fire. She stands very still at the milestone, waiting for her new master, and doesn't look at you at all.
* Wait here for the carriage. -> wait
* Leave her. -> END
endif
if quest.the_grey_mare == rumored
quest the_grey_mare asked
endif
Narrator: A grey mare is tied to the milestone by a halter of black cord. Smoke curls from her mane where it lies on her neck, and when she turns her head there are embers coming up in the backs of her eyes, like fire under ash.
Narrator: On her flank, burned in fresh, is a mark you have seen before: the arms over the gates of the castle on its rock.
if flag.mare_calmed
-> cure_menu
endif
* [if not flag.mare_calm_tried] [Animal Handling DC 14] Calm her before anything else. (one try) -> calm_ok | calm_fail
* [class:ranger] (Talk to her the way you talk to anything wild.) -> calm_ok
* [class:druid] (Talk to her in the old way.) -> calm_ok
* [knows:animal_friendship] (Cast Animal Friendship.) -> calm_ok
* Wait here for the carriage. -> wait
* Leave her for now. -> END

~ calm_ok
set mare_calmed
Narrator: She stops fighting the cord and stands, shivering all over, and lets you put a hand on her neck. Under your palm the hide is hot as a kettle.
interject name:thistle: There, lass. There. Nobody's finishing you tonight.
-> cure_menu

~ calm_fail
set mare_calm_tried
set mare_lost
quest the_grey_mare lost
Narrator: She screams and throws her weight against the cord, and the brand on her flank flares white. When she comes down on all four hooves again there's no grey left in her at all.
Narrator: The coals in her eyes settle and brighten. She looks at you the way the castle looks at the valley.
* Wait here for the carriage. -> wait
* Leave her. -> END

~ cure_menu
Narrator: The brand on her flank is still smoking. Whatever it's doing to her, it isn't finished.
* [knows:remove_curse] (Cast Remove Curse on the brand.) -> cured
* [knows:protection_from_evil_and_good] (Cast Protection from Evil and Good on her.) -> cured
* [if item:holy_water] (Pour a flask of holy water over the brand.) -> cured_water
* [if not flag.mare_rite_tried] [Religion DC 15] (Press a holy symbol to the brand and pray.) (one try) -> cured | rite_failed
* Wait here for the carriage. -> wait
* Leave her for now. -> END

~ cured_water
take holy_water
-> cured

~ rite_failed
set mare_rite_tried
set mare_lost
quest the_grey_mare lost
Narrator: The prayer catches on the brand like a match in lamp oil. Steaua screams, and the white flare runs out from the mark over her whole body and leaves it black.
interject class:cleric: She hates priests. He did say.
* Wait here for the carriage. -> wait
* Leave her. -> END

~ cured
set mare_saved
quest the_grey_mare saved
Narrator: The brand hisses like a doused coal and goes out. The embers in her eyes sink and go dark, and she is grey, all grey, and shaking, and very much a horse.
Narrator: You slip the black halter. She doesn't wait to be thanked: she's a pale streak down the west road toward the camp before the cord hits the ground.
interject tag:kind: Go home, girl.
Narrator: Hooves on the castle road behind you. Too early. A carriage lamp swings up out of the dark, and the black horse in the traces is coming at a gallop.
set carriage_came
approve thistle +2 godrick_pendlebrook +1 liriel_dawnsong +1: You broke the castle's brand on a stolen horse
combat carriage_escort

~ wait
time until 0
set carriage_came
Narrator: Midnight. The carriage comes up the castle road with its lamp swinging and no hand on the reins: one black horse in the traces, and an empty harness beside it, waiting.
if not flag.mare_saved and not flag.mare_lost
Narrator: At the milestone, Steaua stops shivering. When she lifts her head the grey has burned out of her, and her eyes are coals.
set mare_lost
quest the_grey_mare lost
endif
Narrator: The carriage door opens on nothing. Something gets out anyway. Several somethings.
combat carriage_escort
